<h2 id="provision-a-serverless-postgres" class="anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-tighter"><span>Provision a Serverless Postgres</span><a class="rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden" href="#provision-a-serverless-postgres" aria-label="Link to Provision a Serverless Postgres"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3.5"><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.4" d="m3.938 12.688 1.75-11.375M8.313 12.688l1.75-11.375M3.063 4.813h8.75M2.188 9.188h8.75"></path></svg></a></h2>
<p>To set up a serverless Postgres, go to the <a class="group inline" href="https://console.neon.tech/app/projects" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Neon console<span class="whitespace-nowrap no-underline"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="ml-1 inline-block size-3.5! shrink-0 align-[-0.125em]"><path fill="currentColor" d="M0 0h14v14H0z" opacity="0.2"></path><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" d="M9.915 8.885V4.08H5.11M9.625 4.375 4.083 9.917"></path></svg></span></a> and create a new project. Once your project is created, you will receive a connection string that you can use to connect to your Neon database. The connection string will look like this:</p>
<figure class="code-block group/code-block relative flex flex-col [&amp;_pre]:min-w-full rounded-none border border-gray-new-80 dark:border-gray-new-20 [&amp;&gt;pre]:my-0 [&amp;&gt;pre]:rounded-none [&amp;&gt;pre]:bg-white! [&amp;&gt;pre]:py-4 [&amp;&gt;pre]:dark:bg-black-pure! code-wrap" data-has-filename="false" data-line-numbers="false"><pre class="shiki css-variables" style="background-color:var(--shiki-background);color:var(--shiki-foreground)" tabindex="0" data-language="bash"><code class="grid"><span class="line" data-line="1"><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-function)">postgresql://</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-foreground)">&lt;user&gt;:&lt;password&gt;@&lt;endpoint_hostname&gt;.neon.tech:&lt;port&gt;/&lt;dbname&gt;?sslmode=require</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-punctuation)">&amp;</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-foreground)">channel_binding</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-keyword)">=</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-string)">require</span></span></code></pre><button class="invisible absolute right-4 border border-gray-new-80 bg-white p-1.5 text-gray-new-40 opacity-0 transition-[background-color,opacity,visibility] duration-200 group-hover/code-block:visible group-hover/code-block:opacity-100 hover:bg-gray-new-90 dark:border-gray-new-20 dark:bg-black-pure dark:text-gray-new-60 dark:hover:bg-gray-new-8 lg:visible lg:opacity-100 top-[min(1rem,calc(50%-.8175rem))]" type="button" aria-label="Copy"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 16 16" class="h-3.5 w-3.5 text-current"><rect width="8.995" height="9.002" x="5.939" y="5.935" stroke="currentColor" rx="1"></rect><path fill="currentColor" fill-rule="evenodd" d="M2.434.935a1.5 1.5 0 0 0-1.5 1.5v7.001a1.5 1.5 0 0 0 1.5 1.5h1.499a.5.5 0 0 0 0-1h-1.5a.5.5 0 0 1-.5-.5V2.435a.5.5 0 0 1 .5-.5h6.995a.5.5 0 0 1 .5.5v1.5a.5.5 0 1 0 1 0v-1.5a1.5 1.5 0 0 0-1.5-1.5z" clip-rule="evenodd"></path></svg></button></figure>
<p>Replace <code>&lt;user&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;password&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;endpoint_hostname&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;port&gt;</code>, and <code>&lt;dbname&gt;</code> with your specific details.</p>
<p>Use this connection string as an environment variable designated as <code>DATABASE_URL</code> in the <code>.env</code> file.</p>
<h2 id="create-an-ai-agent-with-elevenlabs" class="anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-tighter"><span>Create an AI Agent with ElevenLabs</span><a class="rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden" href="#create-an-ai-agent-with-elevenlabs" aria-label="Link to Create an AI Agent with ElevenLabs"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3.5"><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.4" d="m3.938 12.688 1.75-11.375M8.313 12.688l1.75-11.375M3.063 4.813h8.75M2.188 9.188h8.75"></path></svg></a></h2>
<p>To create a customizable agent, go to ElevenLabs&#x27; <a class="group inline" href="https://elevenlabs.io/app/conversational-ai" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">AI Agents<span class="whitespace-nowrap no-underline"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="ml-1 inline-block size-3.5! shrink-0 align-[-0.125em]"><path fill="currentColor" d="M0 0h14v14H0z" opacity="0.2"></path><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" d="M9.915 8.885V4.08H5.11M9.625 4.375 4.083 9.917"></path></svg></span></a> and then click on <code>Create an AI agent</code> button.</p>
<p><span aria-owns="rmiz-modal-" data-rmiz=""><span data-rmiz-content="not-found" style="visibility:visible"><img alt="" loading="lazy" width="704" height="447" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="" style="color:transparent;width:100%;height:100%" srcSet="/_next/image?url=%2Fguides%2Fimages%2Fpulse%2Fagent-1.png&amp;w=750&amp;q=75&amp;dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7 1x, /_next/image?url=%2Fguides%2Fimages%2Fpulse%2Fagent-1.png&amp;w=1920&amp;q=75&amp;dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7 2x" src="/_next/image?url=%2Fguides%2Fimages%2Fpulse%2Fagent-1.png&amp;w=1920&amp;q=75&amp;dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7"/></span></span></p>
<p>Next, give it a personalized name and select the kind of Agent you would want. For demonstration purposes, let&#x27;s start with a <code>Blank template</code>.</p>
<p><span aria-owns="rmiz-modal-" data-rmiz=""><span data-rmiz-content="not-found" style="visibility:visible"><img alt="" loading="lazy" width="704" height="447" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="" style="color:transparent;width:100%;height:100%" srcSet="/_next/image?url=%2Fguides%2Fimages%2Fpulse%2Fagent-2.png&amp;w=750&amp;q=75&amp;dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7 1x, /_next/image?url=%2Fguides%2Fimages%2Fpulse%2Fagent-2.png&amp;w=1920&amp;q=75&amp;dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7 2x" src="/_next/image?url=%2Fguides%2Fimages%2Fpulse%2Fagent-2.png&amp;w=1920&amp;q=75&amp;dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7"/></span></span></p>
<p>Next, copy the Agent ID displayed just below the customized name of your agent (here, <code>Custom</code>). You will use this Agent ID as the <code>AGENT_ID</code> environment variable in your application.</p>
<p><span aria-owns="rmiz-modal-" data-rmiz=""><span data-rmiz-content="not-found" style="visibility:visible"><img alt="" loading="lazy" width="704" height="447" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="" style="color:transparent;width:100%;height:100%" srcSet="/_next/image?url=%2Fguides%2Fimages%2Fpulse%2Fagent-3.png&amp;w=750&amp;q=75&amp;dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7 1x, /_next/image?url=%2Fguides%2Fimages%2Fpulse%2Fagent-3.png&amp;w=1920&amp;q=75&amp;dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7 2x" src="/_next/image?url=%2Fguides%2Fimages%2Fpulse%2Fagent-3.png&amp;w=1920&amp;q=75&amp;dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7"/></span></span></p>
<p>Next, go to <code>Advanced &gt; Client Events</code> in your Agent settings, and add two events named <code>agent_response</code> and <code>user_transcript</code>.</p>
<p><span aria-owns="rmiz-modal-" data-rmiz=""><span data-rmiz-content="not-found" style="visibility:visible"><img alt="" loading="lazy" width="704" height="447" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="" style="color:transparent;width:100%;height:100%" srcSet="/_next/image?url=%2Fguides%2Fimages%2Fpulse%2Fagent-4.png&amp;w=750&amp;q=75&amp;dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7 1x, /_next/image?url=%2Fguides%2Fimages%2Fpulse%2Fagent-4.png&amp;w=1920&amp;q=75&amp;dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7 2x" src="/_next/image?url=%2Fguides%2Fimages%2Fpulse%2Fagent-4.png&amp;w=1920&amp;q=75&amp;dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7"/></span></span></p>
<p>Finally, go to <a class="group inline" href="https://elevenlabs.io/app/settings/api-keys" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">API Keys<span class="whitespace-nowrap no-underline"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="ml-1 inline-block size-3.5! shrink-0 align-[-0.125em]"><path fill="currentColor" d="M0 0h14v14H0z" opacity="0.2"></path><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" d="M9.915 8.885V4.08H5.11M9.625 4.375 4.083 9.917"></path></svg></span></a>, create an API key and use the value obtained as <code>XI_API_KEY</code> environment variable in your application.</p>
